{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_05385f8d7a9cc631ed358706d5d7b0605b6d4c2f235b4036d0eddbf945489337","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6a253d2ae6102b8ac20888f7a84097ca6301d3001e7705de79ebaf118657c10f","slc_a1305c377284c41913d788e25c101908e077b776f79fd5f46b192c5bed605fcf"],"source_ids":["src_7e3d2ce5f7f45a50a88ddb7655bcafee"],"text":"v0.6.1 consolidated tools: multi_edit merged into file_edit (edits[] for atomic multi-edit), and four checkpoint tools collapsed into checkpoint (save/rewind/restore) and read-only checkpoint_view (diff/list).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_38c61cce565629a074ed964da1c14ca3b000211d5a61d1b1ce1384b368e588e4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3c4fd0703eb2b313838826aeae9a0da5d6acdc23a4d3b0f50d818d80ffc0515e","slc_70d8d9fd3621db403839df4f97e12d28f923b9faa179ee1581f58e547e1fc0ff","slc_8cb6af010012b46b3f4a0c7bfd8da1fdc6126f9e9605585cc59a8751b13aa86b"],"source_ids":["src_78784ab34c0f58be8574d58faed5a3e5"],"text":"Aizen is documented as a single static binary (~34 MB, ~10 ms cold start claimed) requiring no Node, Python, Docker, or cloud account, targeting Windows, Linux, and macOS.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3af7ab718bcdc97d5b61b3ee2be67fce744197e4861011292aebe22c1f89bfbf","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3c4fd0703eb2b313838826aeae9a0da5d6acdc23a4d3b0f50d818d80ffc0515e","slc_68ed27e546b4503253b9b0e4f70b1b0a60a202f5be7e246099d757cc0c35b1fb"],"source_ids":["src_78784ab34c0f58be8574d58faed5a3e5"],"text":"The agent accepts any OpenAI-style /chat/completions endpoint, including OpenAI, OpenRouter, local llama.cpp/vLLM, or an Anthropic gateway.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3ebecac6d2c2ef8b24fdad97feae964bc5f1f9d5f2bb8fca855285e3a2a5899f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_66052295964d7b15257cba9b93d6d4756cdb8dc3ea092cb2184c590fdabc32d0"],"source_ids":["src_b5b6b389adf9566c940070ab77081194"],"text":"Approval (ask/smart/yolo plus a cmd_guard hard floor) is separate from the sandbox: even approved commands get no secrets, no network, and no out-of-workspace writes where kernel backends exist.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5f074ab5b4c50963369dcd51fc8e9853f5571046eb318299442ed63cfdff038e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a4cd5cbe3c76f9eed490fa8b1e5bbd3949a458e1ee5eff0fbd31aef5f355575"],"source_ids":["src_b5b6b389adf9566c940070ab77081194"],"text":"Sandbox modes are auto (default), strict, guarded, and off; strict refuses spawns rather than downgrading, and unattended runs fail closed unless sandbox.allow_guarded_fallback is true.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6f5411b8c7a55f2cf10ddaf47c3f2a726f7e2e064f1c513f8c7aefbd6ddb9e6a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3c4fd0703eb2b313838826aeae9a0da5d6acdc23a4d3b0f50d818d80ffc0515e","slc_8ae272b1eae9b7a40d004341812ae0453c8546c6f50176e495357b77f5903c02"],"source_ids":["src_78784ab34c0f58be8574d58faed5a3e5","src_b5b6b389adf9566c940070ab77081194"],"text":"The sandbox runs commands without inheriting API keys, denies network by default, and enforces filesystem policy via Landlock+seccomp on Linux and Seatbelt on macOS; Windows uses Job-Object containment and reports 'partial'.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7bc1e401d59be4d25fc94a0d810f93d5808a5f468b6e6dcb30c793f993ad1c77","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e83a024e872206ed47554c5b28984b7426cc43a21bfaccfd2433ff2fd7903bc6"],"source_ids":["src_78784ab34c0f58be8574d58faed5a3e5"],"text":"A 'Pantheon' of seven capability-scoped sub-agents (argus, metis, daedalus, nemesis, themis, clio, mnemosyne) is fanned out via `aizen workflow`, which synthesizes one answer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8207e6c9419d8e63eb62d7cba4b27e1c2c5bb05ab922b6e5341db7eaccd769cb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3c4fd0703eb2b313838826aeae9a0da5d6acdc23a4d3b0f50d818d80ffc0515e"],"source_ids":["src_78784ab34c0f58be8574d58faed5a3e5"],"text":"The agent is documented to keep an offline BM25-ranked memory that learns from reuse, plus a persona, a durable 'SOUL' identity, and skills it writes for itself after real work.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_85b8d7c10e6cdeff1f76449391c3adc777b5bb21bb6ba95008d87c03e8a9178b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f55bcc0fe4452817eb80c5a6d59575316fe5fb9860fce7e6a192b049a7bd5cb1"],"source_ids":["src_b5b6b389adf9566c940070ab77081194"],"text":"The sandbox code is organized under src/sandbox with modules for policy, capabilities, a single runner that builds sandboxed commands, audit logging, and per-platform backends (guarded, linux, windows, macos).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8849efd66f1205586c9c2b171e884a4def0e1641644273156c58b9e36c22e55e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1e919b4b4891eeea1ba35ec307e1da2f7b9a81bcf0b5edf87d143a94b8cebd68","slc_6fdbb8217bac8e42ad9bb63dfebc9fd51d10d15bca930dccf29336fc6bc69437","slc_b1f066b8ba0a83708651f7891373de11f02f1da722679af5cf700ebdc6ba19ff","slc_ce181a42e78e4b73ce084f4b5ef0acf0576f3cb15ac02cce8f22e5cb9c876e31"],"source_ids":["src_78784ab34c0f58be8574d58faed5a3e5","src_f607f56cae1f5e7d8b9f0d2d78e1615a"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors sign a CLA once via a bot-comment flow with the exact sentence 'I have read the CLA Document and I hereby sign the CLA'; the CLA grants the maintainer commercial relicensing rights while the public project stays Apache-2.0.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8e621931587e82991be770db96578a73805046d928f621a3aa1aca5ce56e4ee7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"talmetis-labs/aizen@997bdd3bbba4 snapshot 861f8119c0413970","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c1c2bf300f2a0b0216cd6ae4ff382b3124f79d694acb0fb92377574dd6adc1b2"],"source_ids":["src_b5b6b389adf9566c940070ab77081194"],"text":"The sandbox explicitly does not protect against kernel exploits, an already-compromised user account or machine, secrets placed inside the workspace, or a human approving a harmful command.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
